A||N||9||FieroSTETZ||porting exhaust manifolds...||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||01-17-2001||09:51 PM||||anyone documented anny ass-o-meter or other gains from porting the exhaust manifolds? does it change the sound? my manifolds are off so i could get them welded and was thinking about doing a porting job on them , but was wondering if its actually worth it, and if so, what exactly do i do? i have a dremel tool and a die grinder, and would prefer to use the dremel (lower rpm, better control) and was wondering, just grinf it down, or polish the inside of the manifold too? is there any point in me polishing the outside also, or would that just make them look cleaner. thanks for any responses, and i promise i will update everyone when my clutch install is done.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-17-2001||09:57 PM||||They will give you an 8 horsepower gain with some loss in torque. They should look like this after. I had these Jet Hot coated. If you use a Dremal tool if will take you forever. Get an air grinder and some grinding stones. Don't forget to bolt the manifolds to a thick piece of steel so the feet don't warp when you have them welded.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Manifold_opening_6.jpg">  <BR>If you are interested these manifolds are for sale. I am selling them for $300, which includes the crossover pipe. I have $250 into them.<P>If interested give me an e-mail.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||01-17-2001||10:30 PM||||Here's the page I used when I did mine:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-exhaustmanifold.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-exhaustmanifold.html</A> <P><BR>88 gave you the same info that I've heard<P><BR>DXR_DAD<P><BR>||||reg||13
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-17-2001||10:33 PM||||88 Formula,<P><BR>I'm interested in the manifolds & y pipe.  I'll e-mail you. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||01-18-2001||12:07 AM||||Worth it!  Other than basically free horsepower, it will also keep the temps down a little under the hood with less obstructions.  ||||reg||14
Z||000005||DRH||01-18-2001||12:35 AM||||The biggest obstuction is where each runner is welded to the main tube. It's like they didn't make the hole in the main tube big enough.<P>The manifolds are made out of a very hard material. I did mine with a dremel because that's all I had  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I wound up buying a tungsten carbide bit (about $6) to do most of the work and then used grinding stones to smooth it out. The stones don't last long and are VERY slow to try to do the whole job. The carbide bit will last the whole job (and then some) and cuts at a more reasonable rate (still slow). The carbide bit actually chips away tiny slivers of metal. Makes a real mess of tiny little sharp splinters. Wear gloves and cleanup before handling bare handed (I didn't and picked out splinters for a week :O ). DEFINITELY wear safety glasses.<P>An air powered die grinder would probably be MUCH easier.<P>Personally I think it was worth it. Especially if you have them off anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||04-17-2001||05:21 PM||||I picked up an extra front manifold over the weekend.  There wasn't any rear one's at least at that wrecking yard.  I'm going to get a rear one from somewhere and fix them both up.  The front ones first since it's LEAKING! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Ow! that's hot....Ow! that's hot....Ow! that's hot...Will I ever learn?;o)<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||04-18-2001||08:40 AM||||I've heard that porting the exhaust manifolds and the intake manifold results in 6 to 8 hp gain.  I'm not sure porting only the exhaust will give that much.<P>I did the intake and exhaust manifolds when I installed a new Grooms rebuilt long block.  The difference was very noticable between my tired stock 2.8 and the Grooms 2.9 with the intake and exhaust porting.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||04-18-2001||05:05 PM||||1FST2M6 proved it on his dynamometer. He got 8 horsepower and lost some torque.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
